# Secrets Workflow

This repository was configured with the `sops-age` secrets profile.

## Recipients

The generated `.sops.yaml` uses these age public recipients:

$sops_age_recipients_list

Keep age private keys outside the repository. Do not commit decrypted plaintext files.

## Recommended Commands

Prefer running commands with secrets injected into the process instead of writing `.env`:

```bash
sops exec-env secrets/local.sops.env 'uv run <command>'
```

If a tool requires a dotenv file, decrypt as a short-lived local file and remove it when done:

```bash
sops -d secrets/local.sops.env > .env
```

Edit encrypted values with:

```bash
sops secrets/local.sops.env
```

## Rules

- Commit encrypted `*.sops.*` files only when the project intentionally stores encrypted secrets in git.
- Never commit decrypted `.env` files, private age keys, cloud credentials, API keys, or token JSON.
- Keep `.sops.yaml` path rules narrow so only intended files are encrypted.
- Prefer secret references or managed secret stores when encrypted repository files are not required.
